<!-- SECTION: about.About — title -->
<div class="titleband" data-screen-label="About — title"><h1>We&rsquo;re early. Here&rsquo;s exactly <span class="u-1">how early.</span></h1></div>
<div class="introband">
  <h2>The honest state of a new <span class="u-1">movement.</span></h2>
  <p>Uncost is a nonprofit, nonpartisan movement working to lower the real cost of living using evidence, AI, robotics and open tools. It is also, right now, very new &mdash; so here is the honest state of it.</p>
</div>

<!-- SECTION: about.Four parts -->
<div class="u-2 parts4" data-screen-label="Four parts">
  <div class="part4"><div class="pn">01</div><h3>The Movement</h3><div class="pd">Join in — pledge, take part, spread it</div><p>Reach people with visual, sourced explanations, bring them to a trusted front door, and offer clear paths to support, contribute, or partner.</p></div>
  <div class="part4"><div class="pn">02</div><h3>The Case</h3><div class="pd">The evidence — what living really costs</div><p>Define what one human needs, measure what it costs by region, explain the drivers, and publish open methodology.</p></div>
  <div class="part4"><div class="pn">03</div><h3>The Projects</h3><div class="pd">Open tools that cut real costs</div><p>Translate evidence into open software, data tools, planning models, kits, studies, and playbooks that communities and qualified partners can use.</p></div>
  <div class="part4"><div class="pn">04</div><h3>The Assembly</h3><div class="pd">Your voice — transparent and advisory</div><p>A structured, recorded supporter voice through proposals, surveys, and prioritization — within legal, fiduciary, and safeguarding limits.</p></div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION: about.Mechanism -->
<div class="seqhd" data-screen-label="Mechanism"><div class="u-3 metalabel">The mechanism</div><h2 class="u-4">How a cost gets uncosted.</h2></div>
<div>
  <div class="step"><div class="num">1</div><div><h3>Measure</h3><p>Measure the current cost and its context, starting from public data.</p></div></div>
  <div class="step"><div class="num">2</div><div><h3>Publish</h3><p>Publish the sources, dates, methods, and confidence labels — openly, so anyone can check the work.</p></div></div>
  <div class="step"><div class="num">3</div><div><h3>Break down</h3><p>Split the cost stack into its real components: labor, energy, land, materials, waste, market structure, financing, fees, and policy.</p></div></div>
  <div class="step"><div class="num">4</div><div><h3>Match</h3><p>Match plausible AI, robotics, sharing, infrastructure, or public-interest mechanisms to specific components.</p></div></div>
  <div class="step"><div class="num">5</div><div><h3>Package</h3><p>Package the result as open evidence, software, a brief, or a playbook local groups can use. Uncost publishes; local operators decide and act.</p></div></div>
  <div class="u-2 step"><div class="num">6</div><div><h3>Track</h3><p>Track whether total cost actually falls — and publish negative results with the same prominence as wins.</p></div></div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION: about.Principles -->
<section class="blk blk--ink u-block--ink" data-screen-label="Principles">
  <div class="u-5 eyebrow">Working principles</div>
  <h2 class="u-6 sec">Three rules keep it <span class="u-1">honest</span>.</h2>
  <div class="prin">
    <div><h3><i></i>Receipts first</h3><p>Every public number, claim, and cost estimate is sourced, dated, confidence-labeled, and open to correction.</p></div>
    <div><h3><i></i>Open and reusable</h3><p>Models, methods, dashboards, and project designs are public and reusable wherever rights, safety, privacy, and partner terms allow.</p></div>
    <div><h3><i></i>Nonpartisan practical optimism</h3><p>Bold but phased, lawful, measurable, and credible across political identities.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: about.Is / is not -->
<section class="u-7 blk blk--cream" data-screen-label="Is / is not">
  <div class="eyebrow">Plainly</div>
  <h2 class="u-4 sec">What Uncost is — and is not.</h2>
  <div class="isnot">
    <div class="u-8"><h3>Uncost <u>is</u></h3><ul>
      <li>A nonprofit movement to reduce the cost of living.</li>
      <li>A public-benefit technology and evidence platform.</li>
      <li>A community for supporters, donors, volunteers, researchers, builders, planners, and experts.</li>
      <li>A practical bridge from cost-of-living frustration to projects communities can run.</li>
    </ul></div>
    <div class="u-8"><h3>Uncost <u>is not</u></h3><ul>
      <li>A political party or candidate campaign.</li>
      <li>A crypto, DAO, or token project.</li>
      <li>A promise that every physical constraint disappears or that everything becomes free.</li>
      <li>A replacement for local democratic control or qualified professional judgment.</li>
    </ul></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: about.Accountability -->
<section class="blk blk--cream2" data-screen-label="Accountability">
  <div class="eyebrow">Who is accountable</div>
  <h2 class="u-9 sec">What doesn&rsquo;t exist yet.</h2>
  <p class="u-10 lead">We are not incorporated. We have no fiscal sponsor confirmed. We cannot accept donations. The Assembly is not operating. The dashboard is designed, not built. No policy on this site is in force &mdash; every one is a draft awaiting review.</p>
  <p class="u-11 lead"><strong>Who runs it.</strong> Founder-led, with an advisory group forming. Sector and region leads are being recruited. We&rsquo;ll name people when there are people to name &mdash; not before. Where status matters, it&rsquo;s stated: on <a href="/contribute/">Contribute</a>, <a href="/treasury/">The Treasury</a>, and <a href="/policies/">Policies</a>.</p>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: about.Your say -->
<section class="blk" data-screen-label="Your say">
  <div class="eyebrow">What kind of organisation this is</div>
  <h2 class="u-9 sec">You get a genuine say, not a spectator seat.</h2>
  <p class="u-10 lead">Supporters aren&rsquo;t an audience. <strong>The Assembly</strong> is Uncost&rsquo;s structured way to give supporters a real, recorded voice &mdash; proposing ideas, prioritising sectors and regions, and raising objections, one person, one vote, with no payment or donation buying extra weight. Right now the Assembly is advisory: it doesn&rsquo;t run formal votes yet, and won&rsquo;t until its governance policy clears independent review, founder review, and legal review. When it does, individual ballots stay private and outcomes are published.</p>
  <p class="u-11 lead">Our privacy policy states it plainly: we never sell, rent, or trade personal data, and we never use pledge or supporter data for partisan targeting. That&rsquo;s a public draft commitment today, not yet an adopted policy &mdash; but it&rsquo;s the rule we&rsquo;re building to, not a marketing line.</p>
  <p class="u-11 lead">The same principles that run through every number on this site run through how we treat you: receipts first, open and reusable wherever rights and safety allow, and nonpartisan &mdash; we critique systems and policies with evidence, never candidates or parties.</p>
  <div class="btn-row">
    <a href="/assembly/" class="u-btn u-btn--ink">Read the Assembly&rsquo;s standing rules</a>
    <a href="/policies/privacy-data-protection/" class="u-btn u-btn--ghost">Read the privacy policy draft</a>
  </div>
</section>
